Kernel Cache

Copyright © Summon Software Labs

Kernel Cache is an open-source, vendor-neutral runtime for caching compiled and executable AI kernels, compatibility-safe lookup, reuse, invalidation, residency, persistence, and accelerator-aware dispatch across heterogeneous inference infrastructure.

This product is licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0. See the
LICENSE file in this distribution for the full license text.

Kernel Cache does not collect or transmit any telemetry. All telemetry is
written to local files chosen by the operator and never leaves the machine
running the software.

Kernel Cache accepts contributions from individuals and organizations on the
terms of the Apache License 2.0 without requiring a Contributor License
Agreement (CLA). See CONTRIBUTING.md for contribution guidance.
